---
import UseCaseLayout from "../../layouts/UseCaseLayout.astro";
import Steps from "../../components/article/Steps.astro";
import Benefits from "../../components/article/Benefits.astro";
import Note from "../../components/article/Note.astro";
import { Clock, Shield, FileText, Search } from "lucide-react";
---

<UseCaseLayout
  title="Private Client Meeting Notes for Lawyers on Mac | Summit"
  description="Keep client and matter meeting notes on your Mac. No bot joins the call, transcription runs locally, and you choose whether any cloud AI processes the text."
  audience="Legal Professionals"
  current="legal"
  heading="Client meeting notes that stay with each matter"
  lead="Client calls, intake conversations and internal case discussions each belong to a matter. Summit turns recorded conversations into transcripts and summaries on your Mac, with folders to organize matters and search to find what was said."
  ctaHeading="Try Summit on your next client meeting"
  ctaText="Summit runs on macOS. Choose Local Models in AI settings to keep summaries and chat on your Mac."
>
  <h2 class="!mt-0">You choose where client conversations are processed</h2>
  <p>
    Transcription runs on your Mac, and there is no Summit account holding your
    meeting library. Select Local Models and summaries and chat run on your Mac
    too. If you choose a cloud AI provider, it receives transcript excerpts and,
    for chat, your question with related topics, action items and meeting titles
    and dates, so review that setting before recording client conversations.
    Markdown auto-export and iCloud sync are off until you turn them on.
  </p>
  <p>
    Summit gives you control over where data is processed; privilege,
    confidentiality and recording-consent decisions remain yours under your
    professional obligations. The
    <a href="/security/architecture">architecture page</a> lists exactly what is
    stored and what can leave your Mac.
  </p>

  <h2>Keep each matter's notes together</h2>
  <Steps
    steps={[
      {
        title: "Create a folder for each client or matter",
        body: 'Optionally give the folder a <a href="/docs/guides/summary-templates">summary template</a> so intake calls or case meetings are written up the same way.',
      },
      {
        title: "Use clear meeting titles",
        body: "Name meetings with the matter and topic, so the right conversation is easy to spot in search results.",
      },
      {
        title: "Check the scope before you ask",
        body: "Filter search by folder, or select a matter's meetings and chat about just those. The chat shows which meetings are included before you ask a question.",
      },
      {
        title: "Open the original passage",
        body: "Chat answers cite timestamped transcript passages. Check the source before relying on an answer in advice, a filing or a client update.",
      },
    ]}
  />
  <Note>
    Folders help organize notes; they are not a separate account, encrypted
    vault or access-control boundary.
  </Note>

  <h2>A working record, not an official transcript</h2>
  <p>
    Summit transcripts and summaries are AI-generated working notes. They can
    contain errors and are not a certified or verbatim record. Review the
    original transcript or audio before quoting a client or witness.
  </p>

  <h2>Why legal professionals choose Summit</h2>
  <Benefits
    benefits={[
      {
        icon: Shield,
        title: "No meeting bot",
        body: "Summit records from your Mac instead of joining the call as a participant, for video calls and in-person meetings alike.",
      },
      {
        icon: Clock,
        title: "Start from a draft",
        body: "Summit drafts a summary with key points and action items after each recording, so your file note starts from a draft instead of a blank page.",
      },
      {
        icon: Search,
        title: "Recall with sources",
        body: "Search past meetings for specific facts or statements, and follow chat citations back to the passage in the transcript.",
      },
      {
        icon: FileText,
        title: "Export when you choose",
        body: "Export notes as Markdown to the destination you pick, such as a matter folder. Check where that folder syncs before you export.",
      },
    ]}
  />

  <h2>Who it's for</h2>
  <h3>Solo practitioners & small firms</h3>
  <p>
    Take notes from client intake calls, case strategy sessions and witness
    interviews, with a folder for each matter.
  </p>
  <h3>Corporate counsel</h3>
  <p>
    Keep notes from internal consultations, executive briefings and compliance
    reviews, and search them when a question comes back.
  </p>
  <h3>Litigation attorneys</h3>
  <p>
    Record case preparation discussions, client updates and strategy meetings,
    then search a matter's meetings for what was said.
  </p>
  <h3>Transactional lawyers</h3>
  <p>
    Take notes from negotiation calls, due diligence meetings and client advisory
    sessions, and find earlier discussion of deal terms when you need it.
  </p>
</UseCaseLayout>
